      "content": "Leftover debug log statement (`singleFile or includeDir; tarPathPrefix`). Consider removing before merge."
    },
    {
      "path": "pkg/remote/fileshare/s3fs/s3fs.go",
      "start_line": 299,
      "end_line": 299,
      "content": "`log.Printf(\"writing %v\", path)` fires per-entry during tar streaming and will be extremely noisy for large directories. Please remove this debug log."
    },
    {
      "path": "pkg/remote/fileshare/fsutil/fsutil.go",
      "start_line": 31,
      "end_line": 31,
      "content": "Changing `GetParentPathString` to return `\"\"` instead of `fspath.Separator` for the root case is a behavior change. `ReadTarStream` in s3fs uses the result as `tarPathPrefix`; please confirm callers handle an empty string correctly and that this doesn't produce malformed tar paths for top-level entries."
    },
    {
      "path": "pkg/remote/fileshare/fsutil/fsutil.go",
      "start_line": 128,
      "end_line": 132,
      "content": "In `PrefixCopyRemote`, `CleanPathPrefix` is now called on `fspath.Join(destPathPrefix, next.Name)` but the returned `err` is only checked after the `if singleFile { fileName = destPath }` branch. When `singleFile` is true, `fileName` is overwritten with `destPath` but the earlier `err` from the Join-based CleanPathPrefix is still evaluated on the next line — while harmless, the control flow is confusing. More importantly, `CleanPathPrefix` now returns `nil` error for an empty path (changed below), so a genuinely empty computed path will silently pass. Please verify this cannot produce an empty destination key that overwrites the bucket root."
    },
    {
      "path": "pkg/remote/fileshare/fsutil/fsutil.go",
      "start_line": 148,
      "end_line": 152,
      "content": "`CleanPathPrefix` now returns `(\"\", nil)` for an empty path instead of an error. Previously an empty path was treated as invalid. This weakens a guard used across copy/delete paths — an empty prefix passed to S3 list/delete operations could match the entire bucket. Please confirm all call sites still reject empty paths where a non-empty prefix is required (e.g. destination keys)."
    }
  ]
